    "from google.colab import files\n\nuploaded = files.upload()  # Select only used_car_prices.csv.\nfile_path = \"used_car_prices.csv\"\n\n# Stop clearly if the expected dataset was not uploaded.\nif file_path not in uploaded:\n    raise FileNotFoundError(\"Upload used_car_prices.csv from the repository's data folder.\")\n\ndf = pd.read_csv(file_path)\nprint(\"Dataset preview:\")\ndisplay(df.head())\nprint(\"\\n",
    "Dataset dimensions:\", df.shape)\nprint(\"\\n",
    "Column information:\")\ndf.info()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1a4d1579",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Prompts used\n1. **Data analysis prompt:** asks Gemini to explain trends, metrics, relationships, and unusual observations in the CSV.\n2. **Prediction prompt:** asks Gemini to predict the target column for every row, preserve the row identifier, and return only CSV with the identifier and predicted value.\n\n## Important limitation\nThe model's predictions can vary between runs and may be inaccurate. This notebook evaluates predictions against the same rows supplied to the model; it is a demonstration of prompt-based analysis, not a rigorous test of predictive performance on unseen data. A stronger evaluation would reserve a separate test set."
   ]
